{
  "title": "Kestrel Manufacturing – Monthly Close Initiation",
  "path": "engagements/kestrel-manufacturing/close/monthly-close-initiation.docx",
  "document": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 1,
        "text": "Monthly Close Initiation – Kestrel Manufacturing"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "To the Kestrel Manufacturing Finance Team,"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "We are kicking off the monthly close for the upcoming period. Below is the standard close communication and checklist we will follow. Please review the items assigned to you and flag anything that looks off before we get too far in. As always, we want a clean, efficient close — no surprises at the end of the month."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Close Calendar"
      },
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "columns": ["Activity", "Owner", "Due Date"],
        "rows": [
          ["Bank reconciliations (all accounts)", "Elias Finch / CAAS", "Day 2"],
          ["Cash receipts and disbursements posted", "Kestrel AP/AR team", "Day 2"],
          ["Credit card transactions coded", "Kestrel Finance", "Day 3"],
          ["Inventory valuation and variance review", "Kestrel Controller", "Day 4"],
          ["Payroll accruals and allocations", "CAAS Payroll", "Day 4"],
          ["Fixed asset depreciation run", "CAAS", "Day 5"],
          ["Intercompany and loan balances confirmed", "Elias Finch", "Day 5"],
          ["Prepaids and accruals reviewed", "CAAS", "Day 6"],
          ["Revenue recognition check (sales cut-off)", "Kestrel Controller", "Day 6"],
          ["Trial balance and financial statements drafted", "CAAS", "Day 7"],
          ["Management review and commentary", "Kestrel CFO + Elias", "Day 8"],
          ["Final close package delivered", "CAAS", "Day 9"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Checklist"
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": true,
        "items": [
          "Confirm all bank and credit card feeds are pulling through and reconcile to statements.",
          "Verify all cash receipts are recorded in the correct period and deposits tie out.",
          "Review open purchase orders and match invoices received to goods/services delivered.",
          "Run the inventory rollforward; investigate any unusual shrinkage or valuation adjustments.",
          "Accrue payroll through the last day of the month, including bonus and commission accruals.",
          "Post depreciation and amortization for the period.",
          "Confirm intercompany balances between Kestrel entities and the parent match.",
          "Review prepaid schedules and adjust amortization; book any new prepaids.",
          "Revisit accruals from prior month — clear or reverse as appropriate.",
          "Confirm revenue cut-off: goods shipped before month-end are recorded, and no sales after cut-off slipped in early.",
          "Run the trial balance, review unusual fluctuations, and tie out to the general ledger.",
          "Prepare the draft financial statements and variance analysis against budget and prior year.",
          "Deliver the close package and flag any open items for the CFO."
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Notes and Expectations"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "A few reminders to keep this smooth: (1) Please have all source documents uploaded to the shared drive by Day 1; if something is missing, tell us early rather than waiting. (2) We will hold a brief 15-minute check-in on Day 4 to catch any blockers. (3) Anything that lands after Day 6 goes into the following month's close unless it is truly material — let's not stretch the timeline."
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "If you have questions on your assigned items, reach out to me or your CAAS contact directly. We've done this together for a while now, and I know we'll land it clean."
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Thanks — Elias"
      }
    ]
  }
}
